erious concerns? B has strong reliability and stress, but nasty remarks is serious for crew cooperation. That could be disqualifying. A's egocentric and communication difficulty also serious. C's not open to new ideas and show-off also concerning. D's hot temper also concerning.\n\nWhich concerns are more severe? Nasty remarks (B) could affect safety. Hot temper (D) also. Show-off (C) maybe less severe but not open to new ideas is adaptability issue. Egocentric (A) also.\n\nWe might need more info about crew cooperation for each. Could ask other agents. But we need to make a first contribution. Perhaps we can start by highlighting Candidate B's strong reliability and stress, but note concern about nasty remarks. Suggest we need more info on crew cooperation for others. Vote maybe for Candidate B but with reservations.\n\nAlternatively, we could propose Candidate C due to leadership and anticipation, but concerns about openness. Might be okay.\n\nGiven we need to start discussion, we can propose a provisional recommendation for Candidate B, citing strengths and concerns, and ask others for more info on crew cooperation aspects for other candidates.\n\nLet's produce public message: state vote for Candidate B, explain strengths (conscientious, stress handling, weather assessment), concerns (nasty remarks, weak memory). Implication: B is strong but we need to compare with others.\n\nWe also need to include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
